RE4DC (lane discread, 2026-10-15, test 14 item 11): two hang fixes, a settle delay and a DMA completion fix in KallistiOS 804b319
kernel/arch/dreamcast/hardware/cdrom.c. Applied by game/Makefile KOS_DISC_FIX=1 to a build-time copy of the file
(the KOS checkout is not modified).
- cdrom_exec_cmd_timed: on a timeout it called cdrom_abort_cmd() while still holding the G1 ATA semaphore through
  sem_wait_scoped; abort_cmd waits on that semaphore when no DMA is in progress, so the thread blocked forever.
  The semaphore is now released before the abort.
- cdrom_reinit_ex: the CD_CMD_INIT retry loop ran forever while the drive kept answering "disc changed"; 8 tries.
- cdrom_abort_cmd: 100 ms after the BIOS reset + init that follows an abort timeout (GDEMU clones need time after a
  reset before the next CMD_INIT: KOS PR #957).
- cdrom_vblank: a DMA read was declared done once the BIOS command reported completed, while the G1 GD-DMA engine
  (SB_GDST) could still be moving the last bytes; the reader then read the buffer tail early and kept stale lines in
  the operand cache (console 10-15, LinkOrder bench: "invalid prepared enemy effect records"; Flycast never shows
  it). A completed command now ends the wait only with the GD-DMA engine idle (else the DMA end interrupt does);
  cdrom_stream_progress reports a DMA stream transfer in progress while the engine runs (fs_iso9660 32-byte tail).

